From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:02:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/48] net: xpon: omci: send Test result as a notification and
 refuse other tests

G.988 lists Test result (message type 27) among the notifications: it
reuses the TCI of the Test that started it but carries neither the AR
nor the AK bit. The ANI-G result was built with the response encoder and
went out as 0x3b, with AK set.

The agent also answered every Test with success, while only the ANI-G
self test ever produces a Test result. A Test of any other managed
entity (a POTS line test, a circuit pack self test) therefore left the
OLT waiting for a result until its timeout. Answer those with "command
not supported" (result 2), like the other unimplemented actions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 9f025d3..c5b3262 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@
 #define OMCI_MSG_TYPE_TEST_RESULT	27
 #define OMCI_MSG_TYPE_GET_CURRENT_DATA	28
 #define OMCI_MSG_TYPE_SET_TABLE	29
+/* Message type bit 6, acknowledgement */
+#define OMCI_MSG_TYPE_AK		0x20
 
 #define OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS		0
 #define OMCI_RESULT_PROCESSING_ERROR	1
@@ -4522,6 +4524,11 @@ omci_agent_send_ani_g_test_result(struct omci_device *odev,
 					sizeof(pdu), &pdu_len);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	/*
+	 * Test result is a notification (G.988 message type table): it
+	 * keeps the TCI of the Test but carries neither AR nor AK.
+	 */
+	pdu[2] &= ~OMCI_MSG_TYPE_AK;
 
 	omci_agent_log_wire(odev, "TX", pdu, pdu_len);
 	ret = omci_device_xmit(odev, pdu, pdu_len);
@@ -4780,8 +4787,17 @@ omci_agent_build_response_locked(struct omci_device *odev,
 		content[0] = OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS;
 		break;
 	case OMCI_MSG_TYPE_TEST:
-		content[0] = OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS;
-		break;
+		/*
+		 * Only the ANI-G self test produces a Test result; accepting
+		 * any other Test left the OLT waiting for a result that never
+		 * came.
+		 */
+		if (omci_agent_is_ani_g_test(request) &&
+		    odev->ops->get_telemetry) {
+			content[0] = OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS;
+			break;
+		}
+		fallthrough;
 	case OMCI_MSG_TYPE_START_SW_DOWNLOAD:
 	case OMCI_MSG_TYPE_DOWNLOAD_SECTION:
 	case OMCI_MSG_TYPE_END_SW_DOWNLOAD:
